; Binds `(double n)` to `:impl "wasm:double"` exactly as the happy-
; path eval fixture does — `:arity (fixed 1)`. The document calls
; `(double 1 2 3)` so the validator's pre-dispatch arity check fires
; and surfaces `arity_mismatch` against this manifest entry. Used by
; §18's arity-violation stretch case to prove the validator catches
; arity errors before any wasm dispatch.
(plugin :name double :version "1.0.0"
  (expr-func :name double
    :arity (fixed 1)
    :params [number]
    :result number
    :impl "wasm:double"))
